 A common mistake is to start off with while(x<10){, and then somewhere in the middle write x=x+1 (which will change the value of x), then at the end of the loop print x to see the value that it currently has. This will not work as we wish, because after printing x=9 the while loop condition will not be true anymore (x will not be less than 10), and the loop will stop without printing x=10.

